#. Tag: title
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Resumit"

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When moving from &Microsoft; Outlook&reg; to using &kde;'s &korganizer; to "
"manage schedules and appointments, you will probably wish to export your "
"scheduling data from Outlook&reg; and import it into &korganizer;. "
"&Microsoft;'s Outlook&reg; program does provide an export option that can "
"save an appointment to the industry standard vCalendar format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, Outlook&reg; will only export the appointment you have "
"selected, one at a time. This is fine if you only wish to transfer a few "
"appointments, but transferring the 200-300 appointments you may have in your "
"Outlook&reg; folder would not be much fun. Therefore, <ulink url=\"mailto:"
"blueboy@bamafolks.com\">Randy Pearson</ulink> created a small application "
"named <application>Outlook2VCal</application> that can scan and export all "
"the appointments to a vCalendar file at one time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Installacion"

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <application>Outlook2VCal 2.0</application> program is <ulink url="
"\"http://korganizer.kde.org/learning/importdata.html\">delivered as a "
"compress ZIP file</ulink>, which contains a <application>SETUP.EXE</"
"application> application. Merely extract the files using your favorite "
"utility, such as <ulink url=\"http://www.winzip.com\">WinZip</ulink> and run "
"the <application>SETUP.EXE</application> program to install the program on "
"your Windows computer. This should be the same computer where you normally "
"run &Microsoft; Outlook 97&reg;, 2000&reg; or 2002&reg;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on how up to date your system is, you may or may not be prompted "
"to reboot during the installation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the program is installed, you can run it by accessing "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Start</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Programs</guisubmenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Outlook2vCal</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Outlook2vCal</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. You should see this screen appear:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Outlook2VCal main window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Outlook2VCal main window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Outlook2VCal main window</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The program automatically attempts to communicate with Outlook&reg; using "
"OLE Automation. If an error is reported, this probably means you do not have "
"Outlook&reg; installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should first decide if you want to include information about holidays in "
"the exported file or not. Normally you will probably not wish to do this, so "
"the <guilabel>Skip Holidays</guilabel> box is checked by default. Next, "
"click the <guibutton>Export</guibutton> button, which will display a "
"standard <guilabel>File Save</guilabel> dialog box. Browse to the desired "
"folder and enter the filename where you wish to create the new vCalendar "
"data file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Outlook2VCal Save File dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Outlook2VCal Save File dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Outlook2VCal Save File dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the security settings in Outlook&reg;, you may see this screen "
"next. If so, be sure to allow access for a minute or two."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Outlook2VCal Warning message</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Outlook2VCal Warning message</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: outlook-to-vcalendar.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Outlook2VCal Warning message</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
